select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'data-health', 'chapter', 'email-backups-and-site-health', 'Every night the database checks its own records for the mistakes people used to spot by hand, fixes the clear-cut ones itself and lists the rest for you on one card.

## The Data health card

**Today** > **To do**, the Data health card below the usage cards.

1. The card says when it last checked. Press **Check now** to run it again.
2. Each line is one kind of problem with its count, for example "2 Confirmed bookings whose pickup time passed with no pickup recorded". All clear shows "All 17 checks clear."
3. Press a line to open its records. Each record links to its page.
4. Where the fix is safe, the record has its button: **Mark picked up**, **Close**, **Unassign**, **Restart follow-up** or **Close** for a task. The record leaves the card at once.
5. The last line says what was fixed without asking this week.

> Good to know: One in-app notice a day tells Admins when the night''s check found something. It is never emailed or texted.

## What it checks

- Confirmed bookings whose pickup time passed with no pickup recorded (**Mark picked up**), and those whose return time passed and were never closed (**Close**). Both are the same lists and buttons as Bookings > Now.
- Bookings marked expired or declined that were paid or have a pickup or return report. Only you can say whether it really ran: open the booking.
- Cars on rent with no signed agreement or no deposit.
- Real work routed or credited to a test account, and open tasks or leads assigned to someone who no longer works here (**Unassign** sends it back to its queue).
- Real owner leads whose follow-up stopped before they replied, or never started (**Restart follow-up**), and other leads still new after 2 days.
- Licence reviews waiting more than 24 hours.
- Tasks open twice for the same thing, and open tasks whose subject is already settled, such as "Offer expiring soon" for a car that is already out.
- Published cars missing seats, plate, real photos, a rate card or owner terms, and owners with cars and no terms.
- Payments with no booking, and card processor charges that match no payment.
- Deposits still held 7 days after the car came back.
- Offers that expired more than 48 hours ago still in a queue.
- Real people who asked for a sample car and were not offered a real one yet.
- Email or AI usage on course to go over its included allowance.

## Fixed without asking

Every hour, with the task clean-up, the database fixes what needs no judgment:

- A test account on real work is taken off it, and the work goes back to its queue.
- A duplicate task is closed; the copy being worked, or else the oldest, stays.
- A task whose subject is settled is closed, with the reason in its note.

## Test accounts

The site''s nightly checks sign in with test accounts (addresses starting with verify-, and Resend''s test inboxes). They can still sign in, but no real request, lead, task, commission or notice ever goes to one: the database takes them off at once. **People** > **Portals and view as** marks them "Test account"; staff pickers and sales reports leave them out.', 'Data health', 'The nightly self-check on To do: what it finds, the one-tap fixes, what it fixes by itself, and test accounts.',
  'Every night the database checks its own records for the mistakes people used to spot by hand, fixes the clear-cut ones itself and lists the rest for you on one card.

## The Data health card

**Today** > **To do**, the Data health card below the usage cards.

1. The card says when it last checked. Press **Check now** to run it again.
2. Each line is one kind of problem with its count, for example "2 Confirmed bookings whose pickup time passed with no pickup recorded". All clear shows "All 17 checks clear."
3. Press a line to open its records. Each record links to its page.
4. Where the fix is safe, the record has its button: **Mark picked up**, **Close**, **Unassign**, **Restart follow-up** or **Close** for a task. The record leaves the card at once.
5. The last line says what was fixed without asking this week.

> Good to know: One in-app notice a day tells Admins when the night''s check found something. It is never emailed or texted.

## What it checks

- Mercedes-Benz and BMW cars whose model is not a family we know (Model family not recognized): open the car and correct the model, so the Cars filters list it under its family.
